WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:11.623
Kevin is a regular boy in the fifth grade at Hillside Elementary School.

2
00:00:11.624 --> 00:00:16.717
Like most boys his age, he doesn't really like doing his homework.

3
00:00:16.718 --> 00:00:28.183
One day his teacher, Ms. Rose, said, "Kevin, can you come up and write question five from the math homework on the board?"

4
00:00:28.184 --> 00:00:35.728
"Um, well, I, um, well, no," Kevin stammered.

5
00:00:35.729 --> 00:00:41.774
"Why not?" said Ms. Rose. "Where is your homework?"

6
00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:52.777
"Well, you see," replied Kevin, "last night, after I finished my math homework, there was a problem."

7
00:00:52.778 --> 00:00:59.475
"Really? What kind of problem, Kevin?" said Ms. Rose with surprise.

8
00:00:59.476 --> 00:01:04.725
Kevin thought quickly and said, "A terrible problem.

9
00:01:04.726 --> 00:01:14.274
You see, after my family went to sleep, a fire started in my house and my homework was burned."

10
00:01:14.275 --> 00:01:21.098
"A fire! Oh my, was anyone hurt?" asked Ms. Rose.

11
00:01:21.099 --> 00:01:25.715
"Well, actually, my sister was burned a little.

12
00:01:25.716 --> 00:01:33.545
She went to the hospital, but she is okay now," Kevin replied in a brave voice.

13
00:01:33.546 --> 00:01:40.923
A girl named Suzy asked, "Kevin, did your whole house burn down?"

14
00:01:40.924 --> 00:01:49.173
Excitedly, Kevin replied, "Yes, it was a very large fire and the whole house was on fire.

15
00:01:49.174 --> 00:01:55.639
There was smoke everywhere, and the flames were reaching into the sky."

16
00:01:55.640 --> 00:02:01.307
"You must have been very scared, Kevin," said Ms. Rose.

17
00:02:01.308 --> 00:02:05.006
"I sure was," he answered.

18
00:02:05.007 --> 00:02:09.752
"For a moment I thought that I was going to die."

19
00:02:09.753 --> 00:02:16.151
From the back of the room, Ted asked, "How did you get out of your house, Kevin?"

20
00:02:16.152 --> 00:02:22.462
"I got out of my house by . . . by . . . " Kevin thought for a moment.

21
00:02:22.463 --> 00:02:25.901
"A fire fighter came to the window of my room.

22
00:02:25.902 --> 00:02:31.911
He pulled me out onto his ladder and carried me to safety."

23
00:02:31.912 --> 00:02:35.238
Ms. Rose started to become suspicious.

24
00:02:35.239 --> 00:02:41.341
"You are very lucky," she said. "You could have been killed.

25
00:02:41.342 --> 00:02:46.611
By the way Kevin, what time did the fire start?"

26
00:02:46.612 --> 00:02:55.382
"I'm not exactly sure, but I think about 10:30 at night," Kevin replied.

27
00:02:55.383 --> 00:03:02.852
Then Ted shouted, "Hey Kevin, how many fire trucks came to your house to put out the fire?"

28
00:03:02.853 --> 00:03:07.508
"I'd say about five," Kevin replied quickly.

29
00:03:07.509 --> 00:03:12.892
"There were two really big ladder trucks and one truck for the water.

30
00:03:12.893 --> 00:03:17.203
There were also two smaller trucks."

31
00:03:17.204 --> 00:03:21.402
"It must have been very loud," said Ms. Rose.

32
00:03:21.403 --> 00:03:24.735
"Did many people come and watch?"

33
00:03:24.736 --> 00:03:29.657
"Yes, everyone from the neighborhood was there," said Kevin.

34
00:03:29.658 --> 00:03:33.299
"It was very loud."

35
00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:38.225
"How did the fire start?" asked Ms. Rose.

36
00:03:38.226 --> 00:03:40.392
"It started in the kitchen.

37
00:03:40.393 --> 00:03:47.259
There was a cloth that was too close to the oven, and it caught on fire," said Kevin.

38
00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:50.591
Ms. Rose was about to catch Kevin.

39
00:03:50.592 --> 00:03:55.288
"Who was cooking at 10:30 p.m.?" she inquired.

40
00:03:55.289 --> 00:04:02.158
"My mother was cooking," answered Kevin.

41
00:04:02.159 --> 00:04:10.131
"But Kevin, you said that everyone was sleeping when the fire started," questioned Ms. Rose.

42
00:04:10.132 --> 00:04:18.764
"Well, yes, no. I forgot," stammered Kevin.

43
00:04:18.765 --> 00:04:29.830
"And Kevin," said Ms. Rose, "you said it was a loud fire and everyone saw it, but it was not on the news this morning."

44
00:04:29.831 --> 00:04:36.311
"Well, maybe it was too late for the news people," he replied.

45
00:04:36.312 --> 00:04:41.656
"Okay, Kevin," Ms. Rose said, knowing that Kevin was trapped.

46
00:04:41.657 --> 00:04:46.626
"I am going to call your mother to ask her if she needs any help from our class.

47
00:04:46.627 --> 00:04:50.130
Wait just a moment, and I'll be right back."

48
00:04:50.131 --> 00:04:53.986
"No!" pleaded Kevin.

49
00:04:53.987 --> 00:04:56.550
"Why not?" she asked.

50
00:04:56.551 --> 00:05:01.090
"Well, you see, my mother is . . ."

51
00:05:01.091 --> 00:05:05.584
"The truth!" demanded Ms. Rose.

52
00:05:05.585 --> 00:05:13.249
"There wasn't really a fire," Kevin admitted.

53
00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:18.639
"But you told us that your sister was hurt," said Suzy.

54
00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:24.899
"And you told us that you were rescued by a fire fighter," said Ted.

55
00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:31.480
"And you told us that five fire trucks came to your house," replied another boy.

56
00:05:31.481 --> 00:05:38.157
"Kevin is a liar!" shouted all the children.

57
00:05:38.158 --> 00:05:46.723
Ms. Rose looked at Kevin and explained, "Sometimes a small lie can grow into a big lie.

58
00:05:46.724 --> 00:05:48.989
You started with one lie.

59
00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:54.723
Then, because of your first lie, you needed to tell another lie.

60
00:05:54.724 --> 00:05:59.767
Those two lies led to another lie and then another lie.

61
00:05:59.768 --> 00:06:05.123
And this big lie means seven days detention for you, young man.

62
00:06:05.124 --> 00:06:09.840
So what did you learn today?" asked Ms. Rose.

63
00:06:09.841 --> 00:06:15.517
"I should tell the truth," said Kevin in a soft voice.

64
00:06:15.518 --> 00:06:20.406
"That's right. The more you lie, the more you need to lie."
